## summary
No hang in 3/3 runs (each finished in seconds; master and 2.4.4 hang with
z_wr_iss spinning in zio_dva_allocate). Without the degraded-vdev fix the
blocks are still ganged: L0 1600/1600 and L1 2/2 of the 200 MB file, gang
headers and members on the degraded normal vdev d0 (217768 KiB there vs
~204936 KiB without ganging). Metadata blocks <= 4K (spa_min_alloc: L2+,
dnode blocks) get the try_hard pass in the special class and land
unganged on the degraded special vdev d1 (596 KiB vs 560 KiB at creation);
larger metadata (the L1s) fails in special and in normal and is ganged in
the normal class.
